# Example /etc/hosts lines for stable Spark0/Spark1 name resolution.
#
# Copy to (append on each Spark, human-run):
#   /etc/hosts
#
# Use this only if you are NOT relying on mDNS (`*.local`) and you have a stable
# wired subnet. Adjust IPs to match your actual cabling + static leases.
#
# Suggested convention:
#   spark0 = 10.0.0.2
#   spark1 = 10.0.0.3
#
# The DS4 env examples default to `spark0.local` / `spark1.local` for early
# bring-up; if you pin /etc/hosts, update DS4_MASTER_ADDR and DS4_PEER_HOST to
# match the pinned hostnames.
10.0.0.2 spark0
10.0.0.3 spark1
